  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given that from the top&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;of a vertical wall&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;of height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>,</mo></math> the angles of depression of the top&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;and bottom&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;of a vertical tower&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>15</mn><mo>&#8728;</mo></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>60</mn><mo>&#8728;</mo></msup></math> respectively,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;are on the same horizontal level and<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;is a point on&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;such that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mi>B</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">=</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>The required&nbsp;diagram will be</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0001_84421afe0b7c.png\" style=\"width: 383px; height: 202px;\" /></p><p>From the diagram,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>tan</mi><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>30</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p><p>Also,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mn>15</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>30</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>30</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>20</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math></p><p>Now area of the quadrilateral&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>Q</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;area<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>x</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>20</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>)</mo><mn>10</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>600</mn><mfenced><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>Hence, this is the correct option.</p></blockquote>"
